ChromeLLM — notices and source lineage
======================================

ChromeLLM includes project-authored Java 21, C++ JNI and native media code.
Project-authored sources retain their stated SPDX and repository licensing.
This work is derived in part from the upstream Chrome2api project; its
upstream provenance and contributors remain attributable through Git history.

The legacy ChromeML/Chromium/Dawn reference headers, Node adapter, Windows
runner and associated DLLs were removed from the current browserless source
tree in the review candidate. Historical commits still contain prior files,
including DLLs whose redistribution rights were not established. Ordinary
file deletion does not erase those historical Git objects.

No rights to ship Google/Chrome model weights, proprietary ChromeML/Dawn
runtime DLLs, or unrelated model data are granted by this repository.
Treat all historic vendor-owned artifacts as restricted pending audit.

A separately installed, independently licensed llama.cpp checkout and
lawfully supplied GGUF model may be used with the optional new JNI adapter.
Those sources, model weights and any selected GPU libraries retain their
own licenses and distribution requirements.

See LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY.md. Do not infer model or runtime redistribution
rights from historical presence in a Git repository.
